    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute was filed in the no-show category, but the record shows that no no-show (cancellation) fee was ever charged on this trip, so there is no fee of that kind to refund. EV-FARE-00705 itemises the cancellation-fee line at SGD 0.00, and its own money block reports fee_charged SGD 0.00 and driver_compensation SGD 0.00. The SGD 9.40 that was charged is the fare for the completed ride, quoted under the UPFRONT_QUOTE model (quoted_fare_sgd 9.40, total_charged 9.40) and itemised as base SGD 3.80 + distance SGD 2.45 + time SGD 2.35 + platform fee SGD 0.80, which sums exactly to SGD 9.40. There is no arithmetic excess in the ledger.\n\nTo the rider: the trip record EV-TRIP-00705 shows the trip COMPLETED, with cancelled_at, cancelled_by and cancellation_reason_code all null, and the dropoff registered at your home waypoint \u2014 the same waypoint your claim names \u2014 so the ride was performed to the destination you booked. The waiting_time_fee is SGD 0.00 and wait_time_min is 1.0, so nothing was charged for waiting. Your advocate is correct that the four conditions in POL-NS-01 for charging a no-show fee are not made out on this record: there was no cancellation event under limb (d); the 'arrived' marker at 12:12:40 precedes the first trace fix at 12:12:50, so limb (b) is not met; and the in-geofence dwell of 50 seconds (the longest qualifying run, 6 fixes, 12:12:50 to 12:13:40) falls 250 seconds short of the 300-second STANDARD minimum, so limb (c) fails. That establishes only that no no-show fee was chargeable \u2014 and, as it happens, none was charged. The refund POL-NS-06 directs is of the cancellation-fee line, and that line is SGD 0.00, so the shortfall produces no money and does not reach the SGD 9.40 trip fare. Your cash-demand allegation is not documented anywhere: EV-CHAT-00705 holds zero messages and EV-TRIP-00705 records chat_message_count 0 with no in-app calls, and you yourself state that no separate cash waiting payment was made; the driver's statement denies collecting anything beyond the platform-calculated fare. If you wish to raise a driver-conduct complaint about the alleged cash request, that is a separate conduct matter \u2014 it is not evidenced here and it does not make the fare refundable.\n\nTo the driver: your account is accepted. EV-GPS-00705 places you at the pin, with 6 qualifying in-geofence fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 12:12:50 to 12:13:40 and a minimum distance to the pin of 1.13 m, so the POL-NS-02 proximity test is satisfied on admissible fixes. The arrival marker is not caught by POL-NS-05 (you were stationary at the marker, not beyond the 300 m limit or at the 15 km/h threshold), and POL-NS-04 does not apply (no rider messages; no rider track, which that clause treats as neutral).\n\nNo driver compensation arises: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full, and in any event the cancellation fee it would take 80 percent of is SGD 0.00; the anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 110, failing both the 4-or-more and the above-8-percent limbs). No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the abuse and repeat-party counters read zero, the artifacts do not contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, and the deciding facts rest on full-weight COMPLETE artifacts (EV-TRIP-00705, EV-GPS-00705, EV-FARE-00705, all weight 1.0).\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. The filing party's claim is not supported by the evidence and the present state stands \u2014 payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd SGD 0.00 are left as they are. No amount is refunded and no compensation is paid.",
